.TH SDL_const_cast 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_const_cast \- Handle a Const Cast properly whether using C or C++.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_const_cast(type, expression) const_cast<type>(expression)  /* or `((type)(expression))` in C */
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If compiled as C++, this macro offers a proper C++ const_cast<>\[char46]
.PP
If compiled as C, this macro does a normal C-style cast\[char46]
.PP
This is helpful to avoid compiler warnings in C++\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I type
the type to cast the expression to\[char46]
.TP
.I expression
the expression to cast to a different type\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns
.BR expression ,
cast to
.BR type \[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_reinterpret_cast (3),
.BR SDL_static_cast (3)
